  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two **binary** strings AAA and BBB, each of length NNN. Your task is to make your scorescorescore odd which is initially 000 by choosing NNN elements such that:\n\n\nFor each index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), you will select either AiA_iAi​ or BiB_iBi​.\nIf the character you select is equal to \"1\", add 111 to the scorescorescore. If the character is \"0\", add nothing.\nYour goal is to determine whether it is possible to make the scorescorescore an odd number. If it is possible, print `YES`, otherwise print `NO`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT, the number of test cases.\nFor each test case:\n\nThe first line contains an integer NNN, the length of the strings AAA and BBB.\nThe second line contains NNN characters representing the binary string AAA.\nThe third line contains NNN  characters representing the binary string BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line `\"YES\"` if it is possible to make scorescorescore an **odd** number and `\"NO\"` otherwise.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in either uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `\"yEs\"`, `\"yes\"`, `\"Yes\"` and `\"YES\"` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤N≤201 \\leq N \\leq 201≤N≤20",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3×1053 \\times 10^53×105",
      "Ai,Bi∈{0,1}A_i, B_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Ai​,Bi​∈{0,1} for all iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n110\n101\n2\n11\n11",
        "output": "YES\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1:\n\nFor index 111, you have to add 111 to the scorescorescore as both A1A_{1}A1​ and B1B_{1}B1​ are 111.\nFor index 222, you add 111 to the scorescorescore if you select A2A_{2}A2​ (since A2A_{2}A2​ is equal to 111). if you select B2B_{2}B2​ add 000 to the scorescorescore (since B2B_{2}B2​ is equal to 000). Thus, you can add either 111 or 000 to the score for index 222.\nSimilarly, for index 333, you have the option to add either 111 or 000.\nOne possible solution is to select A1A_{1}A1​, A2A_{2}A2​, B3B_{3}B3​ which would result in scorescorescore 333."
      }
    ]
  },
